  "verbalization": "Remifentanil, a full opioid agonist, is linked to Oprm1 through a shared classification in the Full Opioid Agonists category, which includes drugs like Dihydrocodeine, Levorphanol, and Sufentanil. This classification suggests a common mechanism of action involving opioid receptor activation. The Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) between Remifentanil and each of these drugs is the Opioid Receptor Agonist, indicating a shared biological role in activating the Oprm1 receptor. The evidence from these paths collectively supports the notion that Remifentanil, through its inclusion in the Full Opioid Agonists group, binds to and activates the Oprm1 receptor, aligning with the broader pharmacological profile of opioid agonists. The consistency in the LCA and the shared classification across different drugs strengthens the inference that Remifentanil exerts its effects via a mechanism dependent on Oprm1.",
